Anonymous hole-refill regression
================================

Run anon-hole-refill through the platform's 4K userspace ABI launcher on a
kernel with a native 16K page size. The test does not change its page ABI.

  <userpages4k launcher> ./anon-hole-refill
  sudo <userpages4k launcher> ./anon-hole-refill --native-16k

The optional --native-16k argument enables physical density checks and requires
visible pagemap PFNs (CAP_SYS_ADMIN). Without it, four density results are
skipped. Do not use it with a different native page size. Pagemap must be
readable even without privileged PFNs: present bits verify neighbor prefault.

The test owns 16 MiB of logical data. It discards individual 4K leaves and
writes before reading them, exercising missing-PTE refill rather than zero-page
COW. It checks zero initialization, all retained data and neighboring mappings.
Two phased rounds check slot reuse. A two-hole case checks that one fault
prefaults both missing neighbors before the second is accessed.

Initial backing must be within one native page of 16 MiB. Final backing after
each refill sequence must be at most 20 MiB, allowing bounded pool slack. The
old fresh-private-folio path consumes 64 MiB after single-hole refill rounds
and 32 MiB after the paired-hole sequence. Temporary coexistence of original
and replacement backing is allowed; the test does not require 16 MiB at every
intermediate step.

Expect eight TAP results. A 30-second alarm bounds the test. It does not fork,
induce pressure or test concurrent faults; see the companion lifetime tests.
